 "growth_rationale": "No usable 5-year FCF growth rate can be derived from the material, so the field is null. Free cash flow is negative and deteriorating: $105M in 2023, $(5,387)M in 2024, $(14,121)M in 2025 (MARKET DATA), and about $(25,010)M in H1 2026 alone (derived from SEC 10-Q). Percentage growth off a negative base is undefined, and a DCF built on it would not be meaningful. The data that do exist describe a revenue-growth and capex-intensity story, not an FCF growth rate. Revenue grew 34.9% in 2024, 33.2% in 2025 and 53.7% in H1 2026 (MARKET DATA; SEC 10-Q). Analyst consensus has 2026 revenue of $44.68B and 2027 revenue of $113.5B, with a high estimate of $189.46B and a low of $59.42B (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). That consensus implies roughly $32B of revenue in H2 2026 against $12.5B in H1, a ramp the 10-Q does not corroborate. Consensus FCF or capex guidance is not provided. A valuation should therefore be built from explicit revenue, margin and capex-to-revenue assumptions, or from scenarios, rather than from a single FCF growth rate.",
