Filings analysis: {"business_summary":"Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (SPCX; Nasdaq) completed its IPO in June 2026 at $135.00/share, raising $85,675M net (SEC 10-Q). After the February 2026 common-control merger with xAI, it reports three segments: Space (Falcon/Starship launch and Dragon), Connectivity (Starlink: 12.0M subscribers, 10,200+ satellites) and AI (Grok, the X platform, and AI cloud/compute infrastructure) (SEC 10-Q). H1 2026 revenue was $12,508M (+53.7% YoY) with an operating loss of $2,086M and a net loss of $4,817M (SEC 10-Q). Connectivity is the only profitable segment (H1 operating income $2,844M). Space lost $1,204M and AI lost $3,726M (SEC 10-Q). Capex is very large ($28,476M in H1 2026, mostly AI data centers), so free cash flow is deeply negative (SEC 10-Q; MARKET DATA). The market data show a price of $167.55 and a market cap of about $2.21T (MARKET DATA).","key_figures":[{"metric":"Revenue","value":"$7,814M (Q2) / $12,508M (H1); H1 +53.7% YoY vs $8,138M","period":"Q2 and H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Revenue history","value":"$10,387M (2023); $14,015M (2024); $18,674M (2025)","period":"FY2023-FY2025","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Loss from operations","value":"$(143)M (Q2); $(2,086)M (H1)","period":"Q2 and H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Net loss","value":"$(541)M (Q2); $(4,817)M (H1). Q2 EPS $(0.09); H1 EPS $(1.12) including $671M deemed dividend","period":"Q2 and H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Net income history","value":"$(4,628)M (2023); $791M (2024); $(4,937)M (2025)","period":"FY2023-FY2025","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Adjusted EBITDA (non-GAAP)","value":"$3,538M (Q2); $4,665M (H1). Adds back D&A of $5,290M and SBC of $1,470M for H1","period":"Q2 and H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Segment operating income (loss), H1","value":"Space $(1,204)M; Connectivity $2,844M; AI $(3,726)M","period":"H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Operating cash flow","value":"$3,466M (H1 2026) vs $351M (H1 2025)","period":"H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Purchases of PP&E (capex)","value":"$28,476M (H1 2026) vs $6,965M (H1 2025). AI segment $23,551M","period":"H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Free cash flow (derived: OCF less PP&E purchases)","value":"approx. $(25,010)M for H1 2026, derived from $3,466M - $28,476M","period":"H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04) (derived)"},{"metric":"Free cash flow history","value":"$105M (2023); $(5,387)M (2024); $(14,121)M (2025)","period":"FY2023-FY2025","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Capex history","value":"$4,415M (2023); $11,163M (2024); $20,906M (2025)","period":"FY2023-FY2025","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Cash, equivalents and marketable securities","value":"$93,522M cash + $6,487M marketable securities = $100,009M (matches MARKET DATA totalCash)","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04); MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Total debt and finance leases","value":"$39,364M net ($38,433M debt principal + $1,079M finance leases, less $148M deferred costs). MARKET DATA totalDebt is $39,708M","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04); MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Net cash (derived)","value":"approx. $60.6B ($100,009M - $39,364M)","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04) (derived)"},{"metric":"Shareholders' equity / total assets","value":"$127,224M / $192,770M (equity was $2,573M at 31 Dec 2025 before the IPO and preferred conversion)","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Shares outstanding","value":"7,696,293,669 Class A + 5,485,486,276 Class B = approx. 13.18B (as of 28 Jul 2026). MARKET DATA 'shares' covers Class A only","period":"28 Jul 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04) cover; MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Price / market cap","value":"$167.55 / $2,208.6B (market cap equals price x approx. 13.18B total shares)","period":"Market data date","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Enterprise value (derived)","value":"approx. $2,148B (market cap + $39,708M debt - $100,009M cash)","period":"Current","source":"MARKET DATA (derived)"},{"metric":"Valuation multiples","value":"Forward P/E 87.0x; EV/EBITDA 700.4x; Price/Book 17.35; Debt/Equity 0.31; trailing P/E and ROE null","period":"Current","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Backlog / deferred revenue","value":"Backlog $47,461M (56% within 1 year, 34% in 1-3 years, 10% later); deferred revenue $14,286M","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Starlink subscribers / ARPU","value":"12.0M vs 6.0M; ARPU $66 vs $85 per month (Q2)","period":"30 Jun 2026 vs 2025","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"AI nameplate compute draw","value":"1.4 GW vs 0.4 GW","period":"30 Jun 2026 vs 2025","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Customer concentration","value":"Customer A 18.3% and Customer B 19.5% of Q2 revenue. Customer B is in the AI segment","period":"Q2 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Scheduled debt maturities","value":"$944M (rest of 2026), $2,402M (2027), $2,867M (2028), $3,422M (2029), $3,597M (2030), $25,201M thereafter","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Non-cancelable commitments","value":"$27,955M total, of which $22,244M in 2027","period":"30 Jun 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"},{"metric":"Consensus revenue estimates","value":"2026: $44.68B (21 analysts); 2027: $113.5B (22 analysts, +154%); Q3 2026: $12.63B; Q4 2026: $19.67B","period":"FY2026-FY2027E","source":"Yahoo Finance - Analysis"},{"metric":"Consensus EPS estimates","value":"2026: $0.07; 2027: $1.94; Q3 2026: $0.14; Q4 2026: $0.42","period":"FY2026-FY2027E","source":"Yahoo Finance - Analysis"}],"recommended_base_growth_rate":null,"growth_rationale":"No usable 5-year FCF growth rate can be derived from the material, so the field is null. Free cash flow is negative and deteriorating: $105M in 2023, $(5,387)M in 2024, $(14,121)M in 2025 (MARKET DATA), and about $(25,010)M in H1 2026 alone (derived from SEC 10-Q). Percentage growth off a negative base is undefined, and a DCF built on it would not be meaningful. The data that do exist describe a revenue-growth and capex-intensity story, not an FCF growth rate. Revenue grew 34.9% in 2024, 33.2% in 2025 and 53.7% in H1 2026 (MARKET DATA; SEC 10-Q). Analyst consensus has 2026 revenue of $44.68B and 2027 revenue of $113.5B, with a high estimate of $189.46B and a low of $59.42B (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). That consensus implies roughly $32B of revenue in H2 2026 against $12.5B in H1, a ramp the 10-Q does not corroborate. Consensus FCF or capex guidance is not provided. A valuation should therefore be built from explicit revenue, margin and capex-to-revenue assumptions, or from scenarios, rather than from a single FCF growth rate.","growth_sources":["SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04): H1 2026 revenue growth of 53.7%, segment results, backlog, capex, cash flows","MARKET DATA: FY2023-FY2025 revenue, operating income, OCF, capex and FCF history","Yahoo Finance - Analysis: consensus revenue and EPS estimates for 2026 and 2027"],"stated_risks":["AI infrastructure revenue depends on continued AI adoption and is concentrated in a few customers. Cloud services agreements may be terminated by either party on 90 days' notice after an initial ramp period (SEC 10-Q, Item 1A).","Data center delivery risks: physical damage, construction delays, power constraints, supply chain, GPU/equipment shortages, regulatory and permit delays (SEC 10-Q, Item 1A and forward-looking statements).","Customer concentration: Customer A 18.3% and Customer B 19.5% of Q2 2026 revenue (SEC 10-Q, Note 3).","Leverage and covenants: $38,433M of debt principal. The credit facility has a maximum Consolidated Leverage Ratio of 3.75x. A technical default occurred at the xAI acquisition and was waived on 2 Mar 2026 (SEC 10-Q, Notes 9 and MD&A).","Capital intensity and funding: $28,476M of capex in H1 2026 and $27,955M of non-cancelable commitments (SEC 10-Q, Notes 16 and 18). The Spectrum cash payment will use cash or new financing (SEC 10-Q, MD&A).","Spectrum Transaction: about $19.6B of consideration, including about 261.8M Class A shares and up to $8.5B of EchoStar debt payoff. Further payments of $1,241M in 2026 and $828M in 2027 are expected (SEC 10-Q, MD&A).","Acquisition and integration risk: Cursor merger at a $60B implied equity value, paid in Class A shares, expected to close in Q3 2026 and subject to regulatory approvals. Mesh Optical closed 6 Jul 2026 (SEC 10-Q, Note 20).","Litigation and regulatory exposure: EU DSA fine of EUR 120M under appeal; Vidstream patent verdict of $105M plus $67M interest on appeal; Grok image-generation class actions and the Baltimore case; NAACP Clean Air Act suit over Colossus II turbines; Grok.com privacy class action; Dutch GDPR collective actions. A $354M litigation accrual is recorded, and other losses cannot be estimated (SEC 10-Q, Note 16).","Starlink monetization: ARPU fell from $85 to $66 on international expansion and lower-priced plans (SEC 10-Q, MD&A).","Space operations: Q2 mass to orbit fell to 485 metric tons from 652, and Falcon launches fell to 37 from 45. Space segment H1 revenue fell 1.9% with a larger operating loss from Starship spending (SEC 10-Q, MD&A).","Related-party financing: $13,329M of debt for AI hardware under failed sale-leasebacks with Valor, whose CEO is a SpaceX director (SEC 10-Q, Note 17).","Equity overhang and governance: Class B has 10 votes per share. Valor adopted a 10b5-1 plan covering up to 225.9M Class A shares. 1,331M performance/market-condition awards are outstanding (SEC 10-Q, Notes 12, 13 and Item 5).","Valuation: 87.0x forward P/E and 17.35x price to book (MARKET DATA). Consensus EPS revisions are mixed, and the 2027 consensus rests on very rapid revenue growth (Yahoo Finance - Analysis)."],"accounting_red_flags":[{"flag":"Related-party failed sale-leasebacks fund AI hardware outside reported capex","evidence":"Debt of $2,039M current and $11,290M non-current relates to Valor equipment lease agreements, versus $4,507M at 31 Dec 2025. Interest expense to Valor was $513M in H1 2026. $3,921M of PP&E was acquired through 'other financings' (non-cash), and $5,513M of PP&E purchases sit in accounts payable and accrued expenses. Reported cash capex therefore understates total investment. Valor's CEO is a company director.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Notes 9, 17 and cash flow supplemental disclosures"},{"flag":"MD&A says no material debt principal is due until 2031, but the maturity schedule shows about $13.2B due 2026-2030","evidence":"MD&A states 'no material debt principal payments are due until July 15, 2031'. Note 9 schedules $944M (rest of 2026), $2,402M (2027), $2,867M (2028), $3,422M (2029) and $3,597M (2030), totalling $13,232M. These relate to other financings and the failed sale-leasebacks.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), MD&A Debt Agreements vs Note 9"},{"flag":"Large allocation of AI infrastructure costs between R&D and cost of revenue is a judgment call","evidence":"AI segment cost of revenue rose because 'more compute costs [are] being allocated to cost of revenue as our AI infrastructure revenue increased'. AI R&D, which includes data center depreciation, power and cloud costs, was $4,557M in H1 against AI revenue of $3,379M. Reported gross margin and the R&D versus cost-of-revenue split depend on this allocation.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), MD&A AI segment"},{"flag":"AI revenue growth depends on new, short-notice cloud contracts and concentrated customers","evidence":"Q2 AI Solutions & Infrastructure revenue was $2,194M vs $311M, including a $1,600M increase in AI infrastructure revenue from newly offered cloud services. Customer B (AI segment) was 19.5% of Q2 revenue. Contracts are terminable on 90 days' notice after the ramp period, and the identity of Customers A and B is not disclosed. Revenue is recognized over a ramp period and then straight-line.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Notes 2 and 3, MD&A, Item 1A"},{"flag":"Heavy reliance on non-GAAP Adjusted EBITDA","evidence":"Q2 Adjusted EBITDA was $3,538M against an operating loss of $143M. The add-backs are D&A of $2,848M and SBC of $831M. H1 Adjusted EBITDA was $4,665M against an operating loss of $2,086M and capex of $28,476M. MARKET DATA shows EV/EBITDA of 700.4x, and its EBITDA input is not disclosed.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), MD&A Non-GAAP; MARKET DATA"},{"flag":"Large debt extinguishment loss and an unreconciled premium difference","evidence":"Loss on debt extinguishment was $1,545M in H1 (cash flow statement); the notes show $1,526M + $18M = $1,544M. Disclosed prepayment penalties total $425M + $221M + $518M = $1,164M, versus $1,153M in 'Payment of debt extinguishment premium' in the cash flow statement. The xAI debt carried 12.5% rates and was repaid within about 9 months of issuance.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Note 9 and cash flow statement"},{"flag":"Covenant technical default at the xAI acquisition","evidence":"'The Company had a technical default when the Company acquired xAI on February 2, 2026 due to the amount of debt assumed.' A waiver was obtained on 2 Mar 2026.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Note 9"},{"flag":"Common-control mergers recast the historical financials","evidence":"The xAI merger (2 Feb 2026) and X merger (28 Mar 2025) are common-control combinations, and the 10-Q's prior-period amounts reflect the combined entities. Historical figures in MARKET DATA (e.g. FY2025 net loss $4,937M) cannot be reconciled to an audited annual report because none was provided. Pre-merger SpaceX-only trends are not separable.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Note 1; MARKET DATA"},{"flag":"Large unvested performance/market-condition awards not in diluted share count","evidence":"1,331M share-based awards subject to performance and market conditions were outstanding at 30 Jun 2026 versus 13.5M a year earlier. This is about 10% of the 13,176M common shares. A further 564M anti-dilutive SBC securities are also excluded. Terms, grantees and expense recognition are not described in the extract.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Note 13"},{"flag":"Spectrum equity consideration is fixed at $42.40/share, far below the current price","evidence":"About $11.1B of equity (about 261.8M Class A shares at a fixed $42.40) is to be issued at the Spectrum Acquisition Closing. At the market price of $167.55 those shares are worth about $43.9B (derived). The 10-Q does not say whether the intangible asset will be measured at the fixed value or the market value at closing. A prepaid $856M is currently held in Other assets.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), MD&A Spectrum Transaction and Note 6; MARKET DATA (price)"},{"flag":"Cursor option carried at zero, and a compute arrangement with the target","evidence":"The call option on Cursor (a $60B implied equity value deal) was recorded at an initial fair value of zero. The Company also provides Cursor with GPU compute capacity under a Cursor Compute Agreement, with the 'net amount' for Q2 described as 'not material'. Goodwill and share issuance are not yet quantified. Whether Cursor is a revenue counterparty (e.g. Customer B) is not disclosed.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Note 20"},{"flag":"Operating cash flow is supported by working-capital and classification items","evidence":"H1 OCF of $3,466M includes a $2,169M deferred revenue inflow (customer prepayments). Receivables absorbed $2,003M. $1,195M of 'proceeds from product rebates' is classified in investing activities, offsetting capex rather than appearing in operating cash flow. Net loss before non-cash items is large (D&A $5,290M, debt extinguishment $1,545M, SBC $1,470M).","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), cash flow statement"},{"flag":"Segment reporting omits inter-segment revenue, which affects segment profitability","evidence":"Starlink launches do not generate inter-segment revenue; their costs are capitalized in satellites. The Space segment therefore shows an H1 operating loss of $1,204M while Connectivity shows income of $2,844M. Segment results reflect this allocation. No corporate or eliminations column is shown.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), MD&A Space segment description and Note 18"},{"flag":"Internal inconsistency in note disclosure","evidence":"The Note 9 SpaceX Notes par-call spread is 'between 20 and 30 basis points', while MD&A states 'between 0.002 and 0.003 basis points'. Separately, Class B shares are 5,569M on the balance sheet versus 5,485M on the cover page (different dates).","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), Note 9 vs MD&A; balance sheet vs cover page"},{"flag":"Cover-page filing-status response","evidence":"The registrant answered 'No' (☒) to whether it has filed all required reports during the preceding 12 months and been subject to filing requirements for the past 90 days. The reason is not explained. It may reflect the June 2026 IPO, but the 10-Q does not say.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04), cover page"},{"flag":"Third-party data inconsistencies","evidence":"MARKET DATA 'shares' (7.696B) is Class A only, while marketCap implies about 13.18B shares. Yahoo shows 2026 EPS consensus of $0.07 although reported H1 2026 EPS is $(1.12) and Q3+Q4 estimates sum to $0.56. Yahoo also shows 'Year Ago EPS' of $(8.44) and omits Q1 revenue.","source":"MARKET DATA; Yahoo Finance - Analysis; SEC 10-Q (2026-08-04)"}],"data_gaps":["No annual report, 10-K or prospectus (final Rule 424(b)(4)) was provided, so audited FY2023-FY2025 financials, the recast basis for the xAI merger and the historical history in MARKET DATA cannot be verified.","MARKET DATA shows FY2025 OCF of $6,785M, while the 10-Q shows H1 2025 OCF of only $351M. That implies about $6.4B in H2 2025, and no source reconciles this.","No consensus FCF, capex, margin or long-term growth guidance was provided. A forward FCF growth rate is therefore null.","The EBITDA used in the MARKET DATA EV/EBITDA of 700.4x is not given. The ratio implies roughly $3.1B of EBITDA, which is not matched by any 10-Q figure.","Trailing P/E and ROE are null in MARKET DATA, and no TTM figures are provided. Any TTM figure has to be derived by mixing sources.","No Q1 2026 10-Q was provided. Q1 amounts are inferable only as the H1 figures less Q2.","The identities of Customer A (18.3%) and Customer B (19.5%) are not disclosed, so related-party status is unknown.","The terms of the Valor failed sale-leasebacks (rates, maturities, repurchase options, guarantees) are not provided beyond a fixed average rate of 5.9% for 'other financings'.","The terms, grantees and expense recognition of the 1,331M performance/market-condition awards are not provided.","The measurement basis of the $11.1B Spectrum equity consideration, and the expected goodwill and share count for the Cursor merger, are not disclosed.","The composition of the $27,955M in unconditional obligations is not detailed, nor is the share of those obligations that is Spectrum-related.","No Q3 2026 or full-year management guidance is provided in the 10-Q. Analyst estimates (Yahoo Finance - Analysis) are the only forward view, and the 2026 EPS consensus conflicts with reported results.","Yahoo Finance quote data is intraday (12:36 PM EDT, $167.62), while MARKET DATA shows $167.55. Prices are not time-aligned."]}
Qualitative analysis: {"moat":{"rating":"wide","sources_of_moat":["Vertical integration of launch and satellites. SpaceX launches Starlink satellites on its own reusable Falcon rockets. Rivals such as Amazon must buy launches from outside providers at commercial rates.","Scale and head start in LEO broadband. Starlink has 12.0M subscribers (doubled YoY) and 10,200+ satellites. Amazon's Kuiper/Leo has far fewer satellites in orbit.","Network effects and learning-curve economics. Starlink's revenue funds satellite production and launches. The Connectivity segment earned $2,844M operating income in H1 2026.","Regulatory and spectrum positioning. SpaceX is active in many regulatory proceedings that shape the LEO operating environment.","Government and enterprise relationships. Enterprise and government revenue grew 108% YoY, and backlog is $47.5B.","Potential Starship cost advantage. Starship is still unproven commercially, and V3 satellites have not yet flown."],"evidence":"The moat applies to the Space and Connectivity segments, not to the AI segment. Q2 2026 Connectivity revenue was $4.3B (+66% YoY) with $1.7B of operating income. Starlink added a record ~1.7M net subscribers, and ARPU held at $66/month. Launch and Starlink leadership look hard to replicate in the near term. Amazon is the main credible challenger and can bundle connectivity with AWS. The prospectus names 20+ competitors, and some of them are also launch customers. The AI segment (Grok, X, GPU cloud) is built on Nvidia chips bought on the open market, and no durable moat is evident. It lost $3,726M in H1 on $23.6B of capex. The AI segment's Q2 adjusted EBITDA was positive at $1.1B, helped by cloud-services contracts, but its operating loss was still $1.3B. Customer concentration is high: two customers made up 18.3% and 19.5% of Q2 revenue, and one of them is in the AI segment. ARPU fell from $85 to $66 as the mix shifted toward cheaper plans and international markets. The Starship heat-shield fix is management's claim only.","moat_note":"The overall rating is 'wide' only for the launch and Starlink franchise. The consolidated company also carries a large, unproven AI business."},"management":{"rating":"average","capital_allocation":"Operating execution is strong. The company runs a high launch cadence, scaled Starlink quickly, and raised revenue guidance. Management targets a $100B annualized revenue run-rate by December 2026 and has pulled its $1T revenue goal forward to 2030. Capital allocation is very aggressive and unproven at this scale. H1 2026 capex was $28.5B, mostly AI data centers, against operating cash flow of $3.5B, so free cash flow was about -$25B. FCF has worsened each year: +$105M in 2023, -$5.4B in 2024 and -$14.1B in 2025. The balance sheet is strong for now, with about $100B of cash and securities after the IPO and a $25B investment-grade bond issue. Net cash is roughly $60B. Non-cancelable commitments are $27.96B, with $22.2B due in 2027. The CFO claims AI compute capex pays back in under one year, but this is not independently verified. The company plans to build AI compute exclusively on Nvidia chips and to reach over 2 GW by year-end. The February 2026 xAI merger was a common-control deal with a founder-owned entity. It moved a cash-burning AI business into a profitable Starlink franchise. Returns on that capital are unknown. Forward P/E is about 87x and the market cap is about $2.2T, so the valuation leaves little room for capital-allocation mistakes.","governance_concerns":["Dual-class structure. Class B shares carry 10 votes each. Musk holds about 85% of voting power, far above his economic stake.","The board is seen as friendly to Musk and not answerable to IPO shareholders (Morningstar). Texas incorporation and Nevada deal entities may weaken controlling-shareholder protections compared with Delaware.","The xAI merger was a related-party, controller transaction. It raises conflict-of-interest, litigation and regulatory risk. It also adds AI and X-platform content risk, and a possible future Tesla tie-up has been floated.","Key-person and succession risk. Musk runs several large companies at once.","Large related-party and customer concentration. One AI-segment customer made up 19.5% of Q2 revenue.","Q2 results showed heavy AI spending, with $18.4B of quarterly capex. Investors reacted negatively: the shares fell about 8.6% after hours on the day of results and reached an all-time low in the weeks before, though the market data now shows $167.55."]},"industry":{"growth_outlook":"Strong but capital-intensive. Satellite broadband is growing quickly. Starlink subscribers doubled YoY to 12M, with direct-to-cell mobile partnerships (SoftBank, NTT DoCoMo, Spark NZ) and standalone Starlink Mobile expected by the end of 2027. Launch demand is rising. AI compute is the largest and most uncertain growth area, with 1.4 GW of compute in use now and over 2 GW targeted by year-end. Consensus revenue estimates are $44.7B for 2026 and $113.5B for 2027 (+154%). Consensus EPS is $0.07 for 2026 and $1.94 for 2027. Estimates may be unreliable because the company is newly public and merged.","competitive_intensity":"Moderate and rising in connectivity. Starlink has a large lead, but Amazon (with AWS bundling), Eutelsat OneWeb, Telesat and terrestrial and telecom carriers are all competing. In launch, SpaceX is dominant. In AI, intensity is very high. Frontier labs and hyperscalers compete for GPUs, power and talent, and capex requirements are huge.","key_competitors":["Amazon (Kuiper / Amazon Leo, AWS)","Blue Origin","Eutelsat OneWeb","Telesat Lightspeed","Viasat","AT&T / T-Mobile (terrestrial and direct-to-cell)","United Launch Alliance","OpenAI","Anthropic","Google","Meta","Microsoft"]},"catalysts":["Starship Flight 14, the first flight carrying V3 Starlink satellites, plus progress toward an orbital mission with booster catch and reuse","The $6.7B of contracted AI cloud revenue that management says begins ramping in October 2026","Progress toward the $100B annualized revenue run-rate by December 2026, and the Q3 2026 report (consensus revenue about $12.6B)","Starlink subscriber growth, ARPU stability and direct-to-cell mobile launches","Integration of the Cursor team and Grok 4.5 and later model releases","AI capex returns and any capex guidance, which could swing sentiment sharply either way","Index inclusion, lockup expiries and other IPO-related share supply, with dates unknown","Governance or regulatory developments, including related-party transactions and a possible Tesla combination","Amazon Leo deployment pace and enterprise contract wins"],"citations":["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/04/spacex-spcx-earnings-live-updates-q2-2026.html","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/space-exploration-technologies-corp-spcx-050338024.html","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/11/spacex-spcx-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.investing.com/equities/spacex-earnings","https://www.marketbeat.com/earnings/reports/2026-8-4-spacex-stock/","https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SPCX/earnings/SPCX-Q2-2026-earnings_call-692542.html","https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/article/spacexs-first-ever-earnings-report-comes-as-stock-hits-new-all-time-low-q2-preview-132323178.html","https://orbitalradar.com/satellite-internet/starlink-vs-kuiper","https://www.zerohedge.com/technology/spacex-builds-regulatory-moat-around-it-starlink-empire","https://futurumgroup.com/insights/spacex-ipo/","https://www.cnbc.com/2025/07/15/amazon-teams-up-with-rival-musks-spacex-to-launch-kuiper-satellites.html","https://www.esgdive.com/news/institutional-investors-spacex-ipo-governance-concerns-share-structure-board-composition/822254/","https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/spacex-ipo-investors-long-list-unfriendly-shareholder-policies","https://www.dandodiary.com/2026/03/articles/director-and-officer-liability/the-spacex-xai-merger/","https://penchan.co/en/market/ai/spacex/investors-and-partners/","https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260204VL212/spacex-elon-musk-xai-acquisition-merger.html","https://moginlawllp.com/spacex-xai-antitrust-market-consolidation-ai/","SEC 10-Q filed 2026-08-04 (figures taken from the provided filings summary; not re-fetched)"]}
